eak down as: Excise taxes (Highway trust fund) at 6384 with 123 in refunds for a net of 6260, followed by estate and gift taxes at 16844 gross, 5101 in taxes, 66 in refunds, and 5035 net. The next section shows customs duties with 3444 gross, 110 in refunds, and 3334 net, then miscellaneous receipts totaling 3334.\n\nNow I need to identify which column represents the specific net customs receipts value of 5035.\n\nLooking at the table structure, column 7 contains \"Customs duties > Net\" and shows 5035 for the full year 1974. This is the net customs tariff receipts figure I need.\n\nFor the monthly breakdown in 1974, the Customs > Net column displays values ranging from 239 to 355, which sum to 3444 across the twelve months—matching the annual figure exactly. These represent the monthly net customs tariff receipts for each month of 1974. The monthly customs net values for 1974 are 304, 239, 277, 286, 295, 301, 325, 355, 305, 347, 319, and 307. Computing the coefficient of variation using the population standard deviation: the mean is 286.17, and the population standard deviation is approximately 32.17.\n\nDividing the standard deviation by the mean gives a coefficient of variation of around 11.24%.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_50a8a8e8643d4bae8dcc959f","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -A 20 \"1974-Jan.\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1975_03.txt | head -25"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
