d be Net, Gross, Refunds in that order. For 1974 annual: Net=3444, Gross=110, Refunds=3334. The math doesn't reconcile—3444 ≠ 110 - 3334. Let me reconsider what \"Net\" actually represents here. It could be that Gross and Refunds are combined differently, or there's an error in the data. Either way, the monthly and annual values both show this discrepancy, so I should use the Net column directly since that's what's requested.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_cb33f4c4b0f943e5a78a42ef","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport statistics\nimport math\n\n# The correct 1974 monthly Customs (tariff) net receipts values from the table\ndata = [309, 247, 285, 294, 309, 311, 332, 364, 312, 355, 326, 316]\n\nprint(\"1974 Monthly Customs (tariff) Net Receipts (millions of dollars):\")\nmonths = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec']\nfor i, v in enumerate(data):\n    print(f\"  {months[i]}: {v}\")\n\n# Calculate mean\nmean = statistics.mean(data)\nprint(f\"\\nMean: {mean}\")\n\n# Population standard deviation (using statistics.pstdev for population)\nstd_dev = statistics.pstdev(data)\nprint(f\"Population Standard Deviation: {std_dev}\")\n\n# Coefficient of Variation (CV) = (std_dev / mean) * 100\ncv = (std_dev / mean) * 100\nprint(f\"\\nCoefficient of Variation: {cv}%\")\n\n# Round to nearest hundredths\ncv_rounded = round(cv, 2)\nprint(f\"CV rounded to nearest hundredths: {cv_rounded}%\")\n\n# Write to answer file\nwith open('/app/answer.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(f\"{cv_rounded}\")\n    \nprint(f\"\\nAnswer written to /app/answer.txt: {cv_rounded}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
